{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/673117-ephemeral-cover-anchors-and-resonance-influences-or-no-influences","id":673117,"title":"Ephemeral Cover: Anchors and Resonance? Influences, or no Influences?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-21T06:40:08-07:00","id":673117,"title":"Ephemeral Cover: Anchors and Resonance? Influences, or no Influences?","content":"1: This has been asked before, but never really dwelled on when answered, and just left to the realms of handwavium, rather than officially clarified. If the Demon as a Ghost or Spirit has the traits of one, and is able to manifest as such as I will cover further in my next query, then does the Anchor or Resonance condition exist o n anything in order to allow the further manifestation conditions to actually occur?<br /> <br /> 2: I am not sure if I have an older copy of DtD, or not, but I have noticed in the few threads talking about the Ephemeral Cover Exploit, that the common consensus is that a Demon using this Exploit does not have access to Influences. Now, given as they are able to Manifest, and Influences are one of a couple of ways in which they are able to do that, I was wondering if maybe we could get some clarification on whether or not they have them?<br /> <br /> If they don't have access to Influences, then I figure they could just have cultists or anyone else they can manipulate (or even their Ring mates) perform extended actions in order to create the relevant conditions which allow them to manifest, but given as this is a somewhat important aspect of the power, again, I would just like to know for sure whether or not the Demon fully relies upon others in order to be able to affect the physical world in any way beyond Embeds and Exploits.<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1353-riche","name":"RichE","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T07:59:17-07:00","id":673169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichE</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/673117-ephemeral-cover-anchors-and-resonance-influences-or-no-influences#post673117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1: This has been asked before, but never really dwelled on when answered, and just left to the realms of handwavium, rather than officially clarified. If the Demon as a Ghost or Spirit has the traits of one, and is able to manifest as such as I will cover further in my next query, then does the Anchor or Resonance condition exist o n anything in order to allow the further manifestation conditions to actually occur?</div> </div> </div> </div> The Conditions are &quot;created&quot; as part of crafting the Cover. Remember that Cover is nothing more than a really detailed disguise the demons wear - you are not actually a ghost or spirit. The demon, however, must act like there are Conditions, or suffer compromise checks for acting out of character. You don't need those Conditions as more than setting props while you pretend to be an ephemeral entity.<br /> <br /> You are pretending to be a spiritual being, but its all an act. The rules are all handwaved because a demon is just trying to act like one without actually being subject to all the same rules as one.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2: I am not sure if I have an older copy of DtD, or not, but I have noticed in the few threads talking about the Ephemeral Cover Exploit, that the common consensus is that a Demon using this Exploit does not have access to Influences. Now, given as they are able to Manifest, and Influences are one of a couple of ways in which they are able to do that, I was wondering if maybe we could get some clarification on whether or not they have them? </div> </div> </div> If a Cover represents a suitably powerful ghost or spirit that could manifest in certain conditions, then a demon can as well in those same conditions. If you want actual Influences, that's what the Show of Power exploit is for. Or the right selection of Embeds and Exploits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If they don't have access to Influences, then I figure they could just have cultists or anyone else they can manipulate (or even their Ring mates) perform extended actions in order to create the relevant conditions which allow them to manifest, but given as this is a somewhat important aspect of the power, again, I would just like to know for sure whether or not the Demon fully relies upon others in order to be able to affect the physical world in any way beyond Embeds and Exploits. </div> </div> </div> They still have their embeds, exploits, and can make a partial transformation for some demoic form powers. A demon posing as a fire spirit can use Combustion to set fires still. Or use Show of Power.<br /> <br /> When all is said and done, remember that demons are fakers. They don't actually get powers of other supernatural beings, they just try to mimic them with their own abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T09:38:11-07:00","id":673266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/673117-ephemeral-cover-anchors-and-resonance-influences-or-no-influences?p=673169#post673169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They still have their embeds, exploits, and <b>can make a partial transformation for some demoic form powers.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>The creations of Ephemeral Cover are modifications to your demonic form and thus partial transformation is redundant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T10:05:19-07:00","id":673281,"title":"","content":"See? Even better! You still have all your demon form abilities!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T10:25:37-07:00","id":673289,"title":"","content":"That just raises further questions. Because I assumed from this bit of text in the fluff before the mechanics; &quot;Once harvested, the demon stores the Corpus on his demonic form. When the demon assumes this form, the Corpus is visible hanging on his body like a fleshy, translucent cloak.&quot; that they were simply describing how the Demon stores the Corpus while waiting to craft it into a cover; &quot;Once the demon has accumulated enough Corpus (4 x the desired Cover rating), he can craft his spiritual Cover. This requires an extended action (successes required = twice the Cover rating, one roll per hour, Dexterity + Crafts), which must be completed in demonic form.&quot; and the need to be in Demonic form while crafting is because the material is stuck to said form, and has to be shaped into something to mask the form, i.e., be a Cover like anything else, and still not having full access to Demonic Form unless you use the usual rules to access it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1353-riche","name":"RichE","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T11:06:53-07:00","id":673303,"title":"","content":"I personally just treat it like a normal Cover, with all the limits and drawbacks thereof. Don't go reading too much into it - you're a demon who's posing as a ghost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}